{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01363",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.91,
      "end_seconds": 8.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.63,
      "text": "Let me think, you know, hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.06,
      "end_seconds": 14.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "So, come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.19,
      "end_seconds": 25.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Well, I've been having cramping in the calves when I walk. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.23,
      "end_seconds": 30.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.91,
      "end_seconds": 47.99,
      "duration_seconds": 13.08,
      "text": "Yeah, I take metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day. Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast. I take simvastatin, 20 milligrams, maybe, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.59,
      "end_seconds": 55.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.94,
      "end_seconds": 66.13,
      "duration_seconds": 9.19,
      "text": "No, you know, it's at home. Okay, so I used to take glibenclamide, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.72,
      "end_seconds": 71.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Alright, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.6,
      "end_seconds": 75.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Ever since... since this morning, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.21,
      "end_seconds": 81.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Ah. Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.26,
      "end_seconds": 101.91,
      "duration_seconds": 18.65,
      "text": "I, I'd say every other day. Pretty mild, if I'm being honest. It settles a little with stopping. Yes, walking. That makes it worse. I've also had numb patches on both feet, for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.95,
      "end_seconds": 119.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Any foot pain at rest, black skin or pus at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.1,
      "end_seconds": 125.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Let me think, you know, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.71,
      "end_seconds": 131.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Any redness spreading up the foot or smell from the foot at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.9,
      "end_seconds": 135.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.61,
      "end_seconds": 140.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.84,
      "end_seconds": 149.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Hmm, uh, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.85,
      "end_seconds": 153.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.66,
      "end_seconds": 156.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.5,
      "end_seconds": 158.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.59,
      "end_seconds": 162.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.35,
      "end_seconds": 165.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.33,
      "end_seconds": 170.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.12,
      "end_seconds": 187.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.62,
      "end_seconds": 193.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.22,
      "end_seconds": 194.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.43,
      "end_seconds": 197.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Diabetes, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.93,
      "end_seconds": 201.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.6,
      "end_seconds": 207.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "I've had high cholesterol for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.3,
      "end_seconds": 216.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.41,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Okay, I can see diabetes and high cholesterol in your file as well. Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.43,
      "end_seconds": 227.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, yes, I had an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.42,
      "end_seconds": 234.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.64,
      "end_seconds": 239.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Actually, no, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.03,
      "end_seconds": 245.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Okay, shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.77,
      "end_seconds": 257.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.64,
      "end_seconds": 279.84,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 74, SpO2 98 percent on room air, temperature is 36.6 degrees, pressure 171 over 97."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.42,
      "end_seconds": 287.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Okay, I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.43,
      "end_seconds": 292.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.02,
      "end_seconds": 312.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Pulses at the ankle are weak."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.8,
      "end_seconds": 316.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.46,
      "end_seconds": 340.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "There's a small shallow ulcer under the ball of the left foot, no pus or surrounding redness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.44,
      "end_seconds": 343.14,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.87,
      "end_seconds": 349.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.0,
      "end_seconds": 387.4,
      "duration_seconds": 22.4,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. I'd lean towards a diabetic foot ulcer with some circulation concern. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had cramping in the calves when you walk, since this morning, mild, and no smell from the foot or black skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.45,
      "end_seconds": 390.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.0,
      "end_seconds": 401.51,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.65,
      "end_seconds": 409.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Ah, could I get a foot X-ray done? A friend had it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.19,
      "end_seconds": 424.19,
      "duration_seconds": 14.0,
      "text": "So, I wouldn't order it today. If anything changes, we'll reconsider. Okay, there's nothing new for me to start or arrange today. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.02,
      "end_seconds": 433.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Great, you know, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.82,
      "end_seconds": 435.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}